 new bands or edit )TjT* (existing ones. )TjETendstreamendobj75 0 obj2049endobj73 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 59 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 74 0 R>>endobj77 0 obj<</Length 78 0 R>>stream
0.5 w BT/F4 12 Tf0 Tc 0 Tw 108.125 662.5 TD (Diversity Database User Guide)Tj/F4 10 Tf172.776 -530.75 TD [ (1-)1 (6)] TJ/F7 11 Tf-163.776 500 TD [ (De\336)-4 (ne Standards \(optional\))] TJ/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD (If your gel includes molecular weight or other standards, you can enter the )Tj0 -12 TD (values into the computer and apply them on the image.)Tj/F7 11 Tf-9 -27.5 TD (Create Band Sets)Tj/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD (Once you have identi\336ed your experimental bands, you group them into )Tj0 -12 TD (band sets. Band sets contain the positional values of all the unique bands in )TjT* -0.269 Tw (your gels. They are the mechanism by which samples are linked in a database.)Tj/F7 11 Tf0 Tw -9 -27.5 TD (Data Analysis)Tj/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD -0.275 Tw (Once your gel linked to other gels by band sets within a database \336le, you can )Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (use a variety of searching and population comparison tools to analyze your )TjT* (gel images in detail. )Tj/F5 10 Tf90.771 0 TD (Diversity Database)Tj/F6 10 Tf92.688 0 TD ( supports both single lane and )Tj-183.459 -12 TD (multilane sample de\336nition as well as phylogenetic tree and 3-D principle )Tj0 -12 TD -0.042 Tc (component analysis display.)Tj/F7 11 Tf0 Tc -9 -27.5 TD (Print/Export)Tj/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD -0.253 Tw (When your imaging and analysis are complete, you can print out your results )Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (in the form of simple images, images with overlays, reports, tables, and )TjT* -0.015 Tc (graphs. You can export your images and data to other systems for further )TjT* 0 Tc (analysis. )Tj/F7 14 Tf-18 -38.5 TD -0.272 Tw (1.6. Computer Requirements for Running Diversity Database)Tj/F6 10 Tf18 -21.5 TD 0 Tw (Diversity Database will run on a PC as a Windows 95/98/NT 4.0 32-bit )Tj0 -12 TD (application or on a Macintosh as a PowerPC application.)Tj0 -20 TD (The amount of computer memory required for using Diversity Database is )Tj0 -12 TD -0.189 Tw (mainly determined by the size of the images you will scan and analyze. Some )TjT* 0 Tw (images\321particularly those scanned at high resolution\321can be quite large, )TjT* (and your hard disk may quickly run out of space. For this reason, we )TjT* (recommend that you archive images on a network \336le server or some kind of )TjT* (removable storage media after your analysis.)TjETendstreamendobj78 0 obj2353endobj76 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 59 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F5 18 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 77 0 R>>endobj80 0 obj<</Length 81 0 R>>stream
