preference by clicking on the Brackets or )TjT* -0.117 Tw (Lines button next to the Band Style prompt. \(This setting can also be changed )TjT* 0 Tw (in the Band Attributes dialog box.\))TjETendstreamendobj298 0 obj2195endobj296 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 284 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 297 0 R>>endobj300 0 obj<</Length 301 0 R>>stream
BT/F4 12 Tf0 Tc 0 Tw 108.125 662.5 TD (Diversity Database User Guide)Tj/F4 10 Tf169.997 -530.75 TD [ (2-)1 (18)] TJ/F7 12 Tf-169.997 499.25 TD (2.5.c. Application)Tj/F7 11 Tf9 -28.25 TD (Relative Percent Calculation)Tj/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD (The Relative Percent Calculation option allows you to de\336ne how Relative % )Tj0 -12 TD (will be determined for all reports, histograms, and band information )TjT* (functions in Diversity Database: either as a percentage of the signal intensity )TjT* -0.275 Tw (of an entire lane or as a percentage of the signal intensity of the de\336ned bands )TjT* 0 Tw (in a lane.)Tj0 -20 TD (Selecting % of Lane means that the total lane intensity will equal 100 percent )Tj0 -12 TD (and the band that you select will be reported as a fraction thereof.)Tj0 -20 TD -0.196 Tw (Selecting % of Bands means that the sum of the intensity of the de\336ned bands )Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (in a lane will equal 100 percent, and that your band will be reported as a )TjT* (fraction of that sum.)Tj0 -20 TD -0.108 Tw (If you create, adjust, or remove bands with Relative % de\336ned as % of Bands, )Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (the Relative % of all the other bands in the lane will update to re\337ect changes )TjT* (in the total intensity of de\336ned bands.)Tj/F7 11 Tf-9 -27.5 TD (Relative Front Calculation)Tj/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD (The Relative Front Calculation option lets you to de\336ne how relative fronts )Tj0 -12 TD (\(Rf\) will be calculated for lane and band analysis. This is useful if your gel )TjT* (image is curved or slanted.)Tj0 -20 TD (Rf is calculated by dividing the distance a band has migrated from the gel\325s )Tj0 -12 TD (origin by the total distance between the origin and the dye front. These )TjT* (distances can be determined in one of two ways:)Tj0 -20 TD (1.)Tj18 0 TD -0.025 Tc (Drop a vertical line from the origin to the dye front \(Vertical Projection\);)Tj-18 -20 TD 0 Tc (2.)Tj18 0 TD (Measure along the length of the lane \(Follow Lane\).)Tj-18 -20 TD (If a lane is straight and vertical, these methods will give identical results. )Tj0 -12 TD -0.015 Tc (However, the results will differ if a lane is curved or slanted. Choose your )TjT* 0 Tc (preferred method by clicking on one of the two buttons next to the Relative )TjT* (Front Calculation prompt.)TjETendstreamendobj301 0 obj2336endobj299 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 284 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 300 0 R>>endobj303 0 obj<</Length 304 0 R>>stream
BT/F4 12 Tf0 Tc 0 Tw 403.457 662.5 TD (General Operation)Tj/F4 10 Tf-89.335 -530.75 TD [ (2-)1 (19)] TJ/F7 11 Tf-160.997 500 TD (Database Backups)Tj/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD 1.353 Tw (The Database Backups option allows you to specify the number of backup)Tj0 -12 TD 0.967 Tw (database \336les \(0-9 copies possible\) that will be created when you save your)TjT* 0 Tw (databases. )Tj0 -20 TD (If you enter 1 in the \336eld, whenever you save a database, a backup of that )Tj0 -12 TD (database will be saved in a Backup folder in the same directory as the )TjT* (database. The database backup name will be appended with a number 1 )TjT* (\(Windows \336les will also have the extension .dbk\).)Tj0 -20 TD (If you enter 2, the most recent backup will be appended with the number 1 )Tj0 -12 TD (and the next most recent will be appended with the number 2. And so on.)Tj0 -20 TD 0.653 Tw (Backups allow you to recover from mistakes or inadvertent changes to your)Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (database \336le. Specifying a Database Backups value of 0 means that no backup)TjT* (copies will be maintained.)Tj0 -20 TD 0.093 Tw (To open a backup database in Windows, you must change the .dbk extension)Tj0 -12 TD -0.049 Tc 0 Tw (to .ddb using Windows Explorer.)Tj/F7 12 Tf0 Tc -18 -24.25 TD [ (2.5.d. T)55 (oolbars)] TJ/F6 10 Tf18 -20.75 TD (These settings determine the behavior and positioning of the secondary )Tj0 -12 TD (toolbars and Quick Guides.)Tj0 -20 TD (If the Show Diversity Database Quick Guide checkbox is selected, the )Tj0 -12 TD (Diversity Database Quick Guide will open automatically when you open )TjT* (Diversity Database.)Tj0 -20 TD (If Align Quick Guide with Document is selected, the Quick Guides will pop )Tj0 -12 TD (up \337ush with the edge of your documents. Otherwise, they will appear \337ush )TjT* (with the edge of the screen.)Tj0 -20 TD (Quick Guide Placement and Toolbar Placement determine which side of the )Tj0 -12 TD (screen the Quick Guides and toolbars will \336rst open.)Tj0 -20 TD -0.369 Tw (The Placement Behavior setting determines whether a Quick Guide or toolbar )Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (will always pop up in the same place and format \(Always Auto\), or whether )TjT* (they will pop up in the last location they were moved to and the last format )TjT* (selected \(Save Prior\).)TjETendstreamendobj304 0 obj2334endobj302 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 284 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 303 0 R>>endobj306 0 obj<</Length 307 0 R>>stream
BT/F4 12 Tf0 Tc 0 Tw 108.125 662.5 TD (Diversity Database User Guide)Tj/F4 10 Tf169.997 -530.75 TD [ (2-)1 (20)] TJ/F6 10 Tf-151.997 500.5 TD -0.014 Tc (The Toolbar Orientation option buttons specify whether toolbars will \336rst )Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tc -0.32 Tw (appear in a vertical, horizontal, or expanded format when you open Diversity )TjT* 0 Tw (Database.)Tj0 -20 TD (Tool Help Delay allows you to specify the amount of time \(in seconds\) the )Tj0 -12 TD -0.018 Tc (cursor must remain over a toolbar icon before the Tool Help appears. First-)TjT* 0 Tc -0.177 Tw (time users may want to specify a short delay to learn the names of the toolbar )TjT* 0 Tw (functions, while experienced users can specify a longer delay once they are )TjT* (familiar with the icons.)Tj0 -20 TD -0.025 Tc (Tool Help Persistence determines how long the Tool Help will linger on the )Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tc (screen after you move the cursor off a toolbar icon.)Tj/F7 14 Tf-18 -38.5 TD (2.6. User Settings)Tj/F6 10 Tf18 -21.5 TD (If Diversity Database is on a workstation that has multiple users, each user )Tj0 -12 TD (can have his or her own set of Diversity Database preferences and settings.)Tj0 -20 TD (In multiple-user situations, Diversity Database\325s preferences and settings are )Tj0 -12 TD -0.019 Tc (associated with individual user names. On a PC with Windows 95/98/NT, )TjT* 0 Tc (your user name is the name you use to log onto the computer. On a )TjT* (Macintosh, your user name is the Owner Name under the File Sharing \(OS )TjT* (8.x\) or Sharing Setup \(OS 7.x\) control panel.)Tj/F12 9 Tf-18 -20 TD (Note:)Tj/F6 10 Tf36 0 TD (If you do not log onto your PC under Windows 95/98 or do not have a )Tj0 -12 TD (Owner Name on your Macintosh, then you do not have a user name and )TjT* (your preferences and settings will be saved in a generic \336le.)TjETendstreamendobj307 0 obj1871endobj305 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 284 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F