BT/F4 12 Tf0 Tc 0 Tw 458.128 662.5 TD [ (T)55 (utorials)] TJ/F4 10 Tf-144.006 -530.75 TD [ (3-)1 (35)] TJ/F6 10 Tf-151.997 500.5 TD (This completes Lesson 3. If you want to use this tutorial again, close the open )Tj0 -12 TD (image and database without saving. All changes you have made to the \336les )TjT* (will be lost.)Tj/F7 11 Tf-9 -27.5 TD (Important Points to Remember About Matching)Tj/F6 10 Tf9 -20.5 TD (Band modeling can take some practice. When modeling, remember these )Tj0 -12 TD (general points:)Tj0 -18 TD (\245)Tj18 0 TD -0.315 Tw (After you have identi\336ed a \336rst lane and created an initial band set, study )Tj0 -12 TD 0 Tw (the band modeling lines and look for patterns of identi\336cation across the )TjT* (lanes.)Tj-18 -16 TD (\245)Tj18 0 TD (If a band has been misidenti\336ed by auto-matching, the best method to )Tj0 -12 TD (correct this is to change the accurately modeled bands around it from )TjT* (matched to known \(red to green\) as described in step 8 above. This )TjT* (improves the overall modeling, and is better than trying to change the )TjT* -0.031 Tc (band directly, which can disrupt the modeling.)Tj-18 -16 TD (\245)Tj18 0 TD 0 Tc (Be careful about identifying new band types. If you see a yellow band in )Tj0 -12 TD (the same position across three or more lanes in the gel, it is probably safe )TjT* (to call it a new band type.)Tj-18 -16 TD (\245)Tj18 0 TD (When identifying a new band type, select a lane near a standard lane to )Tj0 -12 TD (create the new band type \(as noted in step 6 above\).)Tj-18 -16 TD (\245)Tj18 0 TD (If you \336nd that previously matched bands are reverting to unknown )Tj0 -12 TD -0.403 Tw (when you try to match, you may be forcing the modeling lines out of their )TjT* 0 Tw (appropriate pattern. Recheck the modeling lines, and make sure they )TjT* (follow those connecting the standards.)Tj/F7 14 Tf-36 -38.5 TD (3.4. Lesson 4. Building and Searching the Database)Tj/F6 10 Tf18 -21.5 TD (In this lesson, you will add a gel image to a preexisting database and then )Tj0 -12 TD -0.357 Tw (learn some techniques for searching the database. \(See Chapters 5 and 10 for a )TjT* 0 Tw (more detailed explanation of the commands described in this lesson.\))Tj0 -20 TD (1.)Tj18 0 TD (Start by opening Image.3. This image has lanes and bands already )Tj0 -12 TD (de\336ned on it. To view these, click on the Show Overlays button on the )TjT* (main toolbar.)TjETendstreamendobj761 0 obj2478endobj759 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 681 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 760 0 R>>endobj763 0 obj<</Length 764 0 R>>stream
