or suppressing salt-and-pepper )Tj-93.864 -12 TD 0 Tw (noise; its effect on Gaussian noise is minimal. This \336lter calculates the )Tj0 -12 TD -0.466 Tw (mean of the pixel values in the \336ltering window, including the pixel being )TjT* 0 Tw (processed. If the difference between the mean and the individual pixel )TjT* (value is above a certain threshold, then the individual value is replaced )TjT* (by the mean.)Tj-18 -16 TD (\245)Tj/F5 10 Tf18 0 TD (Median.)Tj/F6 10 Tf40.078 0 TD ( Also useful for suppressing salt-and-pepper noise, this \336lter )Tj-40.078 -12 TD -0.123 Tw (calculates the median value of the pixels within the \336ltering window and )Tj0 -12 TD -0.147 Tw (uses it to replace the value of the pixel being processed. The median \336lter )TjT* 0 Tw (produces very little blurring if a small-sized window is selected.)TjETendstreamendobj1208 0 obj2859endobj1206 0 obj<</Type /Page/Parent 1191 0 R/Resources <</Font <</F4 16 0 R /F5 18 0 R /F6 20 0 R /F7 25 0 R /F12 82 0 R >>/ProcSet 2 0 R>>/Contents 1207 0 R>>endobj1210 0 obj<</Length 1211 0 R>>stream
